| `test_quality.assertions.exempt.<test>` | string | keel and a generated project carry two entries, for the two tests of `tests/unit/models/test_budget.py` whose function returns None; absent, `{}`, which its reader reports as `[using default] test_quality.assertions.exempt = {}` | a test's function-level pytest node id, `<path>.py::<name>` or `<path>.py::<Class>::<name>`, mapped to a non-blank reason | `tests/assertion_quality.py` (`policy`, `verdict`), called by `tests/integration/test_assertion_quality_gate.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `test_quality.assertions.exempt` row | Lets the named test through the assertion-quality gate: for a test that passes by not raising and has no result to assert. An entry whose test the gate does not fail, or that names no test, is stale and fails the gate. A blank reason, a key with no `::` or a parametrized id fails the gate with `SourceTreeError`, preserving the loader's diagnostic lines and naming this key. | a test that has a result to assert: assert it | always |
